9.  MUTATION CONTROLS.
======================================================================================================================
  cluster     kernel res  Newtonian res
  Pal 4           -0.874         -0.216
  Pal 14          -1.306         -0.494
  Pal 3           -0.844         -0.033
  NGC 2419        -0.211         -0.021
  [PASS] M1 MUTATION CONTROL, and it is the cleanest statement of the whole claim: switch the kernel off (nu = 1, pure Newton with baryons only) and the globular clusters land ON zero while the dwarf spheroidals at the same internal acceleration stay far above it.  The cluster deficit IS the kernel's boost and nothing else, and the pipeline is not manufacturing it -- the identical pipeline gives the dwarfs a large positive residual   (Newtonian median: clusters -0.124 dex, dwarfs over the same x_i +1.021 dex on N=12; with the kernel on, clusters -0.859 and dwarfs +0.114)
  [PASS] M2 MUTATION CONTROL on the DATA: inflating every measured dispersion by sqrt(2) must move every residual by exactly +log10(2) and nothing else in the pipeline may respond   (shifts ['+0.301029996', '+0.301029996', '+0.301029996', '+0.301029996'] against +0.301029996)
  [PASS] M3 MUTATION CONTROL on the THEORY: raising a_0 a hundredfold drives every cluster deeper into the modified regime, so the predicted dispersions rise and the residuals must fall further below zero   (median -0.859 dex at the canonical a_0, -1.820 at 100 a_0)
  [PASS] M4 the independent Gauss-Legendre quadrature reduces to the framework's own isolated kernel exactly when the external field is switched off, so the two implementations agree on the thing they are both meant to compute   (boost_sphere(x_i, 0)/nu(x_i) = 1.000000000000)

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT
======================================================================================================================
  THE CLAIM SURVIVES IN SUBSTANCE AND CARRIES ONE WRONG NUMBER.

  Reproduced independently: Pal 4 -0.874, Pal 14 -1.306, Pal 3 -0.844, NGC 2419 -0.211, median -0.859 dex,
  against dwarf spheroidals over the same internal accelerations at +0.114 dex on N = 12.  Object-by-object
  depth matching -- not the 2.1-dex window g05 used -- leaves a median gap of +0.948 dex with every cluster
  below its own depth-matched dwarfs.  The sign survives Upsilon_V = 1, the higher disputed Pal 14 dispersion,
  the Milky Way's measured rotation curve as the external field, and all three stacked (-0.388 dex).  Under
  nu = 1 the clusters land on zero and the dwarfs do not, so the deficit is the kernel's boost and not the pipeline.

  THE ERROR.  g05's Upsilon_V = 1 caveat, quoted as -0.558 dex, applies the NEWTONIAN mass scaling (+log10 2)
  to a deep-MOND prediction.  Three of the four clusters sit at x_i = 0.013-0.061 where sigma_pred goes as
  M^(1/4), so the shift is +0.151 dex.  The exact value is -0.678 dex, not -0.558.  The error is against
  g05's own interest and does not touch the claim's substance, but the quoted number is wrong.

  THE PROCEDURAL VIOLATION.  Section 4e runs the canonical footing only.  Repaired here: with the dwarf set
  held fixed the alt footing gives clusters -0.896 and dwarfs +0.075, a gap of +0.972 dex against the canonical
  +0.973 -- identical to 0.002 dex.  Nothing was hidden.  But the '+0.114 dex on N = 12' dwarf number is
  fragile to the WINDOW EDGE: x_i scales as 1/a_0, so re-applying the fixed 0.01-1.2 window on the alt footing
  re-selects the sample and reads -0.007 on N = 11.  Quote the GAP, never the absolute dwarf offset.

  THE DEEP-MOND LIMIT IS NOT UNIFORM.  Pal 3 and Pal 4 are isolated deep-MOND and radius-independent, so the
  model-derived r_h,l does not matter for them.  Pal 14 is EXTERNAL-FIELD DOMINATED (x_i/x_e = 0.67), where the
  kernel is quasi-Newtonian with a boosted G and the prediction depends on the radius again: 25 per cent in
  r_h,l moves Pal 14's residual by 0.09 dex.  The cluster carrying the most extreme residual is the one whose
  structural input is both model-derived and load-bearing.

  THE WEAK POINT, AND IT IS NOT THE ONE g05 NAMES.  g05 names Pal 14's 16 stars.  The real soft spot is that
  the depth-matched gap collapses to +0.198 dex at NGC 2419 -- the only cluster with real statistical weight
  (183 velocities), the only one whose boost is small (1.55), and the only one outside the deep-MOND limit.
  The claim is carried by three clusters with 16-23 stars each, two of whose dispersions are N-body model fits.

  THE PHYSICS OF THE FORK IS USED CORRECTLY, WITH ONE FRAMING DEFECT.  Modified inertia is a class with no
  unique prediction, so it has no predicted SIGN for a dispersion-supported system; S5's setup sentence gives
  the alternative a prediction it does not have.  The falsification that does go through is weaker and enough:
  a single-sign 'pressure support breaks the kernel' hypothesis predicts one sign and the data show two.  g05's
  verdict block already says the fork itself is untouched, and that is the correct standing.

